To further improve performance in concurrent environments, consider implementing a thread-safe cache for frequently used keys and IVs. Additionally, use asynchronous I/O operations where possible to avoid blocking the main thread during decryption processes.

Remember to write unit tests covering various edge cases, such as invalid keys, IVs, padding modes, and corrupted data, to ensure the robustness of your library.']

